(4 TECHNICAL SPECIFICATION — CONCRETE AND REINFORCEMENT) Tj T*
(\(a\) Plain and reinforced cement concrete works shall comply with IS 456:2000.) Tj T*
(\(b\) Grade of concrete for all RCC members shall be M30.) Tj T*
(\(c\) The nominal cover to reinforcement shall be 45 millimetre. Maximum free water-cement ratio) Tj T*
(shall be 0.55.) Tj T*
(\(d\) Cement content shall be not less than 320 kg/cu.m.) Tj T*
(\(e\) OPC 43 grade cement complying with IS 8112 shall be used.) Tj T*
(\(f\) Fe 500D TMT reinforcement bars complying with IS 1786:2008 shall be used.) Tj T*
(\(g\) Mix proportioning of concrete shall be done as per IS 10262:2019.) Tj T*
(\(h\) Concrete shall be cured for not less than 10 days.) Tj T*
(\(i\) Mechanical needle vibrators shall be used for compaction of concrete.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5 TESTS AND INSPECTION) Tj T*
(\(a\) Testing of concrete for compressive strength shall be done as per IS 516:1959.) Tj T*
(\(b\) The contractor shall furnish manufacturer's test certificates for every lot of cement and) Tj T*
(reinforcement.) Tj T*
(\(c\) Before despatch, the Engineer-in-charge will inspect the equipment at the maker's works.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6 DOCUMENTATION, WARRANTY AND TRAINING) Tj T*
(\(a\) Detailed shop drawings are to be submitted by the contractor for approval not later than 21) Tj T*
(calendar days after the award of work.) Tj T*
(\(b\) On completion the contractor shall hand over three copies of the O&M manuals.) Tj T*
(\(c\) The contractor shall guarantee the whole installation for 12 months after handing over) Tj T*
(against faulty design, materials and workmanship.) Tj T*
(\(d\) Operation and routine maintenance training shall be given by the contractor to the) Tj T*
(Department's operators.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
